--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived from rspaargaren/iown-homecontrol-esp32sx1276 (Apache 2.0)
https://github.com/rspaargaren/iown-homecontrol-esp32sx1276
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * iohc_flipper/src/iohc/hmac_1w.c
    `compute_checksum()` is a verbatim port to C of `computeChecksum()`
    from src/iohcCryptoHelpers.cpp:92-102.

  * iohc_flipper/src/iohc/key_encrypt.c
    `iohc_wrap_install_key()` is an algorithmic port of `encrypt_1W_key()`
    from src/iohcCryptoHelpers.cpp. The public iohc transfer_key constant
    `34c3466ed88f4e8e16aa473949884373` originates from line 47 of the same
    file.

  * Protocol field structure documentation for cmd 0x30 (1W install-key
    broadcast) — its 16-byte enc_key + 1-byte man_id + 1-byte data + 2-byte
    seq layout — comes from docs/commands.md in the related
    rspaargaren/iown-home documentation project.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Other acknowledged sources (no code reused, concept / documentation only)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Velocet/iown-homecontrol (CC0 1.0 public domain)
    https://github.com/Velocet/iown-homecontrol
    General protocol documentation and io-homecontrol command-ID reference.
    No attribution required by license; cited here as good practice.

  * merbanan/rtl_433 (GPL-2.0-or-later)
    https://github.com/merbanan/rtl_433
    Conceptual reference for sub-GHz sync alignment when the hardware sync
    detector locks one byte early. No code copied — algorithm reimplemented
    independently for the CC1101 path.

  * DarkFlippers/unleashed-firmware (GPL-3.0)
    https://github.com/DarkFlippers/unleashed-firmware
    Host firmware. iohc-flipper is a dynamically-loaded user application
    (FAP), not statically linked against the firmware. The Flipper
    community treats FAP-to-firmware as a library boundary and permits
    permissive licenses for FAPs.

